    "citations": [
      "700"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Eleven studies on birds in Europe found negative or no effects from agri-environment schemes.",
    "citations": [
      "700"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Three reviews from the UK reported population increases of cirl buntings, corncrakes and Eurasian thick-knees after the introduction of specially-designed agri-environment schemes.",
    "citations": [
      "172"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "For plants, 7 out of 11 studies from five European countries found agri-environment schemes maintained or had little or no effect on plants, plant diversity or species richness.",
    "citations": [
      "700"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Three studies on plants in Europe found increases in plant species richness, while two studies found decreases.",
    "citations": [
      "700"
    ]
  },
  {
